US CIA and US State Department Behind Serbia's "Student List" Media N1 and Nova S (United Group) [video]<p><a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50300051">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50300051</a><p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J5lwZU7Q5U0" rel="nofollow">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J5lwZU7Q5U0</a><p><pre><code>    US government-funded pro-opposition outlet BIRN through its Media Ownership Monitor Serbia project admits the central Student List media channels - N1 and Nova S - were created by former US director of the CIA David Petraeus via KKR and former US Ambassador to Serbia Cameron Munter; 

    The parent United Group was acquired and the media platforms built up from 2013-2014 onward as the center of opposition media in Serbia opposing Serbia’s existing leadership and institutions, and playing a central role in both “student protests” last year and the “Student List” movement this year; 

    United Group was only recently (earlier this year) acquired by Alpac Capital, but KKR still maintains an undisclosed amount of shares </code></pre>
with the move a likely an attempt to distance US involvement in the media network;<p><pre><code>    When “leaderless” and “decentralized” protests are praised in the Western media, scroll down in the article where they eventually admit who the leaders and organizations are behind them, perform a simple internet search to identify the key people and investments making them possible to determine whether a movement is indigenous or the product of foreign interference;</code></pre>
